* GITVOCDROP - the engine op, as a SUBROUTINE.  See qm/BP/GIT.QM.
*
* One line of glue, exactly as jBASE's DEFC wrappers are: the handlers in BP/
* call these by name on their ENGINE arm, so the same handler source works
* here unchanged.  All the CCALL machinery is in GIT.QM.
*
* THE WORD THE PREPROCESSOR READS IS NOT WRITTEN IN THIS COMMENT, deliberately.
* A conditional directive inside a comment is a portability trap of its own,
* and the suite greps for sources that TEST a symbol without including
* PLATFORM.H -- which a comment naming one would fail, for no reason.
*
* TWO ARGUMENTS, AND THE OP IS VOCDROP.  This wrapper used to take three and
* send PRUNEGONE, which is a different operation entirely -- so a wholesale add
* would have called it with the wrong arity against the wrong engine function.
* GIT.OBJ calls it as GITVOCDROP(list, out); the repository is supplied here,
* exactly as GITFURNITURE supplies it, and for the same reason.
      SUBROUTINE GITVOCDROP(LIST, ANS)
      CALL GIT.QM("VOCDROP", ".git", LIST, "", "", "", ANS)
      RETURN
END
